/.vs
/src/Presentation/Api/appsettings.Development.json
ANALYZE.md

# Runtime-uploaded user content (LocalFileProvider's write target, wwwroot/Files/<container>/) - never belongs
# in source control. Found live 2026-08-22: 4 stray committed files here caused a real, recurring production
# bug - every deploy recreated them (and their containing directory) owned by the GitHub Actions runner's own
# UID (1001), which has no matching account on the deploy target, blocking new uploads until manually chown'd
# - and the fix kept reverting on every subsequent deploy, because these files came back every time.
/src/Presentation/Api/wwwroot/Files/

# Same class of bug as wwwroot/Files/ above, found 2026-09-02: GlobalService.GenerateSiteMapAsync (a daily
# Hangfire RecurringJob, Startup.cs) deletes and regenerates every file under wwwroot/sitemap/ at runtime -
# 16 files were committed here, so every run/deploy produced a spurious diff, and reflected whatever local/
# dev database happened to be attached at the time rather than real content.
/src/Presentation/Api/wwwroot/sitemap/
